{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1216410-scion-world-of-darkness-crossover","id":1216410,"title":"Scion / World of Darkness Crossover?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-07T18:33:39-07:00","id":1216410,"title":"Scion / World of Darkness Crossover?","content":"I been thinking a lot..not only system wise but plotwise rather.<br /> would it be feaseable for a unnofficial crossover? how do you think the games would mesh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T22:57:28-07:00","id":1216507,"title":"","content":"Has potential. Sounds less cringingly last-season-of-Xena-esque than the WoD/Exalted crossovers people perennially yammer about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T23:53:21-07:00","id":1216517,"title":"","content":"I did it, but in 1st ed Scion there were a lot of issues in general, and setting wise. I wouldn't do it for 2nd ed. But there is a lot of cool glamour to it. Like now it opens up the options for followers and guides. Like we had a child of the Morgan with a Corax Morgan Guide, and I had a player who was a Childe of Samedi with Risen Followers. That part was very cool and satisfying. Also opened up the depth of Antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T17:21:50-07:00","id":1218367,"title":"","content":"Would Scion not sit better with chronicles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","name":"Rathford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T01:53:21-07:00","id":1218443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1216410-scion-world-of-darkness-crossover?p=1218367#post1218367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Scion not sit better with chronicles?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. The charm is the heavy history of the Classic World of Darkness and their many mythic ties, like Baba Yaga existing, Set Existing, Fenris Existing. The Chronicles don't have as much of this, like most of the Gamelines have a more Universal take, like Werewolf Tribes existing everywhere in Foresaken while the Apocalypse Tribes have very specific history like the Pure Tribe encountering the Wymbringers with the European colonization. CWOD has specific Characters who affect history, and lots of specific Mythological references, while Chronicles often downplayed individual NPCs in history and often specifically contradicted Myth. Like in the Underworld Book a powerful Underworld God isn't really Mictlan or Hades he is more of an Allgod that isn't a specific one, such a being wouldn't work as well in Scion. And their Settings are more of places with their own brand new mythology/history that doesn't really mesh with world myths like how the Dominions of the Underworld aren't really regional underworld myths, just weird places that are all over the place, while the CWOD had the Dark Kingdoms which specifically were split by Paradigms of Cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}